Phase 11 – Release Readiness (Deployment Section) UI/UX & Backend Re-Architecture

Objective

Completely redesign and stabilize the Release Readiness → Deployment section.

The objective is to:

* simplify the UI,
* remove redundant information,
* improve usability,
* reduce screen clutter,
* correctly reuse Settings page Kubernetes connections,
* validate deployments accurately,
* verify deployment freshness using Git SHA,
* and ensure all frontend/backend APIs work correctly.

This is a mandatory implementation. Existing working functionality must not regress.

⸻

Acceptance Criteria

1. Remove Redundant Connection Status

Current Problem

Release Readiness currently shows:

* GitHub Connection
* iTrack Connection
* Kubernetes PROD Connection

These are already displayed in Generate Report.

This duplication wastes screen space.

Required Changes

* Remove the entire top Connection Status panel from Release Readiness.
* Do NOT remove it from Generate Report.
* Generate Report remains the only page that displays GitHub/iTrack/Production connection validation.

⸻

