12. Verify Deployment Freshness Using Git SHA

This is a major enhancement.

Current deployment validation only checks whether deployment exists.

This is insufficient.

Scenario:

* Branch cut completed
* Test deployment completed
* Stage deployment completed
* Another developer commits to Release branch afterwards

Deployment still exists.

But latest code is NOT deployed.

Current implementation incorrectly reports deployment as valid.

⸻

Required Validation

For every deployment:

Read:

Deployment

↓

Pod

↓

Labels

↓

Latest Git SHA deployed

Then compare against:

Latest Git SHA available on Release Branch

If both SHAs match:

Deployment is current.

If SHAs differ:

Deployment is stale.

⸻

13. Deployment Status Messages

Instead of generic status, provide meaningful messages.

Examples:

✅ Environment is up-to-date

⚠ Deployment is behind Release Branch

⚠ Latest Release commit has not been deployed

⚠ Redeployment required

Choose concise, user-friendly wording.

Avoid technical jargon where possible.

⸻

14. Compare Against Latest Release Commit

Deployment validation should compare against:

Latest commit on Release Branch

NOT

Previous production SHA

NOT

Previous deployment SHA

Always compare deployment against current Release Branch head.

⸻

15. Detect Post-Deployment Commits

System must detect this scenario:

1. Release deployed
2. Deployment completed
3. New commit pushed to Release Branch

Deployment immediately becomes outdated.

UI should clearly indicate:

Deployment requires redeployment because newer commits exist.

⸻

